From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Oliver Sargison <sargo@sargo.cc>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 18:59:23 +1300
Subject: [PATCH 53/54] Plutonium: ext-image-copy-capture-v1 in Exo, for grim

EXO-CAPTURE: ext-image-copy-capture-v1 with ext-image-capture-source-v1's
output sources. Each frame is a copy of the output's root layer written
into the client's shared-memory buffer (XRGB8888 or ARGB8888), with full
damage. A session starts once the embedder allows it
(exo::wayland::ImageCaptureDelegate): PlutoniumCapture asks the user as for
the portal ("capturerequest" to the focused shell, else Ash's picker),
needs both switches on (it can be a screenshot or a recording), and
publishes it as a capture of kind "wayland" that any shell can stop. A
client that goes away while asked cancels the request (its picker
closes). No toplevel sources (Exo has no foreign toplevel list), no
cursor: a cursor session's capture session stops at once, and no dmabufs
(wl-screenrec wants its encoder's tiled ones, which need a GPU copy).
exo::Buffer gains a getter for its handle. The capture source protocol's
target generates ext-foreign-toplevel-list too, which its toplevel
sources refer to.
